  ,transcribed into music braille from
    the print edited by ,ferruccio
    ,busoni for the ,franz ,liszt
    ,foundation1 ,breitkopf and ,hartel1
    ,leipzig1 #aiaa1 plate ,f4,l4 #da4
    ,the first edition 7,leipzig3
    ,kistner1 #ahdi7 was consulted where
    the print is unclear4  #bjbf4

  ,transcriber's notes4
  ,bar-over-bar format4 ,the right-hand
    part carries the upper staff and the
    melody1 the left-hand part the
    staves below it4 ,where the print
    divides an arpeggio between the
    hands1 it is written in the
    left-hand part1 and a hand sign
    inside the part shows where the
    other hand takes over4
  ,unnumbered groups in the print are
    written as tuplets of their size1
    filling a half measure in the
    arpeggios 7fourteen sixteenths1 or
    twelve to eighteen thirty-seconds7
    and a beat in the sextuplets4 ,three
    thirty-seconds before a dotted
    eighth in measure #gj are written in
    the time of two4
  ,measures #bi1 #cg1 #eb1 #fa and #gj
    hold cadenzas or fermatas and are
    longer than the measure4 ,a music
    comma ends a group of short notes
    before a longer one4
  ,octaves marked #h in print are
    written at pitch4 ,slurs over the
    arpeggios and fingerings are
    omitted4

